{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"content_hash":"449c8781c81b80560c48d438c5f04ae254ee1b517926c90172df054d3bb4a434","digest":{"component_or_area":"autodeploy script","key_entities":["infra/scripts/autodeploy.sh","tests/scripts/test_autodeploy_disk_pressure.py","rebar-autodeploy.timer","prune_docker_caches","reclaim_under_pressure","root_disk_pct","DISK_PRESSURE_PCT","PRESSURE_PRUNE_MIN_INTERVAL","PRESSURE_PRUNE_TS_FILE","BUILD_CACHE_KEEP","AUTODEPLOY_DISK_PRESSURE","rebar-root-disk-pressure","/etc/rebar/autodeploy.env"],"problem_keywords":["disk pressure","docker prune","root disk full","autodeploy","no-op tick","garbage collection"],"propositions":["Root disk on review-bot stays at 92-96% pressure during autodeploy quiescence because prune_docker_caches only runs on deploy and backoff paths, not on the no-op early exit (~2-min cadence).","The prune_docker_caches function is defined after the no-op exit line, making it unreachable from that call site; it must be relocated above the no-op exit to enable pressure-triggered pruning.","A pressure-triggered, throttled reclaim hook on the no-op path with absolute threshold (DISK_PRESSURE_PCT default 80%) and min-interval throttle (PRESSURE_PRUNE_MIN_INTERVAL default 600s) prevents disk saturation while avoiding churn.","The new reclaim path must emit a countable AUTODEPLOY_DISK_PRESSURE marker via the existing marker() function and remain non-fatal (prune failure does not alter autodeploy exit code)."]},"digest_hash_version":1,"model":"bedrock:us.anthropic.claude-opus-4-8","schema":"ticket_digest_v1"},"env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","event_type":"TICKET_DIGEST","timestamp":1787760644541788001,"uuid":"ab879345-57f5-486b-8f15-bbd2a21a8c9f"}